Patch-Source: not yet submitted upstream; certauth has had no commit since
2019 and https://github.com/ikreymer/certauth/issues/23 (the same pyOpenSSL
breakage) has been open and unanswered.  To be filed at
https://github.com/ikreymer/certauth/issues

pyOpenSSL 26.4.0 removed X509Req, X509Extension, PKCS12, load_pkcs12 and
X509.add_extensions, which leaves certauth completely non-functional -
CertificateAuthority() cannot even be constructed.  Replace pyopenssl with
cryptography throughout.

Notes on behaviour changes:
- The CSR built in generate_host_cert() is dropped, it only carried the
  public key into a certificate signed by the CA.
- Serial numbers now start at 1, cryptography rejects a zero serial number.
- Host certificates get an authorityKeyIdentifier.  Without it OpenSSL 3.5
  rejects them with "Missing Authority Key Identifier", which defeats the
  point of the package.
- CertificateAuthority now hands out cryptography objects instead of
  OpenSSL.crypto ones.  pyOpenSSL's SSL.Context.use_certificate() and
  use_privatekey() accept both, so wsgiprox keeps working.

